Z||000051||84Bill||06-18-2001||12:21 AM||||Just wanted to put up an edited picture of the "Fiero traffic jam" I managed to get my hand edited out of the picture with very good results. For those of you that want it as a desktop let me know what size you want and I can format it to your screen size.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR> <IMG SRC="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero/Shows/Mech/image048.jpg"> <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero/Shows/Mech/image47E11.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 06-18-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000052||ChadMan||06-18-2001||09:30 AM||||Hey skitime, thanks for the link to those air horns.  Were they hard to wire up at all?  My 88 Coupe has the wimpy single Sunbird horn instead of the cool dual horns most Fieros had.||||reg||14
Z||000053||84Bill||06-18-2001||10:44 AM||||I don't know what Ski did but that compressor really needs a lot of juice. I spliced the hot from the cooling fan just before the fan relay. I tried to use standard gauge wire but it started to SMOKE  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> if I held the horn on to long. Thats when I got wise and used a fuelpump relay and heavier wire  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <BR>I don't think you can just plug the compressor directly into the existing system, I know mine will fry the wireing very quickly if I did.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000054||ChadMan||06-19-2001||08:44 AM||||I was afraid of that!  Thanks, Bill.||||reg||9
Z||000055||skitime||06-19-2001||09:03 AM||||Chadman, I have used horns like these on several car and only switched the plug from the stock horn to the air horn. I think 84Bills must be a bigger air compressor or something because I have had no problems with this air compressor drawing too much current. The one he listed drives three horns and this one only drives two horns. This horn is a lot less expensive too. I have used them for years without a problem. The compressor is mounted at the same location as the stock horns (stock horns are still mounted but disconnected) The horns are bolted to the plastic inner wheel well with the end of the horns coming out just below the well.  It is an easy simple install.||||reg||1
Z||000056||84Bill||06-19-2001||09:10 AM||||I would tend to agree with Ski on this one. Since two horns require less air, his compressor will draw less current than mine.<BR>For 18 bucks it's worth a try  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
